WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:06.599
The final volume of Stranger Things 4 is loaded
with easter eggs, from secret Eggos to fantasy

00:00:06.599 --> 00:00:09.559
swords, Stephen King, Back To The Future,
and Pulp Fiction.

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:14.370
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing the biggest, best,

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.990
and most epic details hidden in the Season
4 finale!

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.530
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:25.610
The sword that Hopper picks up for his face-off
against the Demogorgon in Russia is no ordinary

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:30.650
weapon, it's the legendary Atlantean sword
wielded by Conan The Barbarian.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:34.660
If you were wondering how on earth the sword
ended up there, there's a little clue in the

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.089
seventh episode when the prisoners were given
access to a weapons cabinet just before their

00:00:39.089 --> 00:00:40.730
fight against the monster.

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:45.699
Look carefully as Dmitri grabs a spear, but
one of the others takes the sword behind him.

00:00:45.699 --> 00:00:50.579
And there was a tease in the opening episode
of Season 4 to us getting some Conan The Barbarian

00:00:50.579 --> 00:00:55.579
action later via the poster for the Schwarzenegger
movie in Mike's bedroom.

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:59.780
When Hopper and Joyce come across a room in
the prison full of demogorgons and demodogs

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:05.199
submerged in giant vats of liquid, the moment
has strong echoes of Alien Resurrection, which

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:10.670
co-stars Winona Ryder and features [her and]
a cloned Ripley discovering a lab full of

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.000
tanks containing various xenomorph experiments.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.640
There's also an easter egg to the second Alien
movie when Sullivan orders his men to split

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.250
up to look for Eleven…

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:21.580
Quarter and search by twos.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.920
Hicks, take the upper level.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.170
This is a nod to Dwayne Hicks from Aliens
who was also ordered to do the same thing…

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.390
Quarter and search by twos.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:31.080
Plus, when Paul Reiser's Owen calls El "kiddo"…

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:32.080
Hey, kiddo.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:35.390
…it's a nod to the way his character Burke
addresses Ripley in Aliens.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.270
That's a second chance, kiddo.

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:43.200
On top of that, David Harbour has said the
third Alien movie was a big influence for

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.480
Season 4 and the way the demodog chases Hop
through the corridors is reminiscent of the

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:52.030
xenomorph chase in Alien 3, as well as Bob's
fate in Season 2.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:56.149
And Hopper's plan to bait one of the demodogs,
then lure the others into a trap for Murray

00:01:56.149 --> 00:02:01.200
to flame them in the prison pit, is a reference
to Alien 3 where the prisoners lure the xenomorph

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.799
into a trap.

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:03.859
Eddie and his B.C.

00:02:03.859 --> 00:02:07.850
Rich Warlock guitar play a crucial role in
the season finale.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:12.780
Notice how the red crackle finish on the guitar
mirrors the Upside Down's colours, with its

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.530
red and black and its cracks of lightning.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.670
She was destined for an alternate dimension.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:23.390
In fact, the classic heavy metal guitar was
customised by the show's crew from a regular

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:24.390
black design.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:29.790
Although the Metallica song Eddie plays is
actually about drug addiction, its title "Master

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:35.030
of Puppets" fits how Vecna toys with his victims,
manipulating them like they're puppets on

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.260
a string.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:40.311
And many of its lyrics that we hear during
the show tie in well with the Creel House

00:02:40.311 --> 00:02:42.040
sequence that it accompanies.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:47.750
For example, 'I'm your source of self-destruction'
and 'Where's the dreams that I've been after',

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:53.390
fit how Vecna uses the memories of his victims
against them, as he tries to do with Max again

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.950
here, bringing back memories of Billy trapped
in the sauna.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:01.890
Interestingly, even some of the song's lyrics
that don't make it into the show, like 'Twisting

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:07.340
your mind and smashing your dreams / Blinded
by me, you can't see a thing', are also spot

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.590
on for Max's story.

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:14.019
There was also a heart-breaking clue to Eddie's
eventual demise at the hands of the Upside

00:03:14.019 --> 00:03:18.870
Down's demobats during the D&amp;D game in the
first episode, because if you look really

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:22.360
closely, you can spot a tattoo of bats on
his arm.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:27.549
Also, this tattoo of a clawed hand controlling
a puppet was another clue to the song "Master

00:03:27.549 --> 00:03:31.010
of Puppets" that Eddie ended up playing in
the finale.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.760
And just before he dies, Eddie tells Dustin…

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:37.129
You're gonna have to look after those little
sheep for me, okay?

00:03:37.129 --> 00:03:41.549
…a reference to how he saw The Hellfire
Club as a place for those like Mike and Dustin

00:03:41.549 --> 00:03:42.549
who didn't fit in.

00:03:42.549 --> 00:03:43.959
I knew it the moment I saw you.

00:03:43.959 --> 00:03:47.019
You sat on that table right over there, looking
like two little lost sheep.

00:03:47.019 --> 00:03:51.960
There's a fantastic visual homage to the opening
scene of Star Wars when Sullivan and his men

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.299
storm into the Nina facility.

00:03:54.299 --> 00:03:58.700
The way they blow open the door, followed
by a gunfire battle through a steam-filled

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:03.439
corridor is incredibly reminiscent of the
Stormtroopers busting open a doorway and having

00:04:03.439 --> 00:04:05.319
a shoot-out with the Rebel guards.

00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:10.810
Then the way Sullivan strides down the hallway
looking for El parallels Darth Vader arriving

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:16.090
in the aftermath of the battle demanding to
know where the Death Star plans are.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:19.889
And the Duffer Brothers have specifically
said they "wanted to capture the tone" of

00:04:19.889 --> 00:04:22.210
The Empire Strikes Back for Season 4.

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:26.940
So, there's Eleven not wanting to complete
her training with Brenner and instead go and

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:31.530
help her friends in Hawkins, a reference to
how Luke Skywalker leaves his training with

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:34.120
Yoda early to help Leia and Han Solo.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:39.130
Plus, there's the way the season ends with
the villain's triumph as the Upside Down breaks

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:40.870
into the real world.

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:45.090
And one of our amazing Movie Lovers points
out that Max ending up in a coma brings to

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.440
mind Han Solo being captured and frozen in
carbonite.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:53.139
And there's another hat-tip to the galaxy
far, far way when Murray utters one of the

00:04:53.139 --> 00:04:56.090
franchise's famous lines:
I don't know, Jim.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:57.930
I got a bad feeling about this.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:04.550
…as they roll up to the Russian prison to
break back in only to find no guards on watch.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:09.530
After Vecna's pain finally releases the vines
that are strangling and about to kill Robin,

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.699
Nancy, and Steve, Robin responds…

00:05:11.699 --> 00:05:15.200
I don't believe in a higher power or divine
intervention.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:19.630
But that was a miracle.
…which is a shout-out to how Samuel L. Jackson

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:25.800
and John Travolta miraculously survived a
hail of bullets in Pulp Fiction, which also

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:29.069
starred Uma Thurman, the mother of Robin actress,
Maya Hawke.

00:05:29.069 --> 00:05:30.100
This was divine intervention.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:34.140
As Nancy is getting the cleaning supplies
together for the gang to clear up the old

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:38.520
cabin in the woods where Hop and El used to
live, there's a very brief shot of a packet

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.540
of Eggos.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:43.520
Eleven's favourite food since Mike first gave
them to her back in Season 1.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.880
Whatever you want, kiddo.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:45.889
It's on me.

00:05:45.889 --> 00:05:46.889
Waffles, please.

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:52.030
After Vecna succeeds in opening the four gates
to the Upside Down in Hawkins, the ground-splitting

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:56.430
cracks converge in the middle of the town,
right next to the Clock Tower.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:01.900
Given all the clock symbolism in Season 4,
this location doesn't feel like a coincidence.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:06.139
It might also be a reference to the importance
of the Clock Tower in Back To The Future,

00:06:06.139 --> 00:06:09.900
where it was a crucial way of harnessing the
energy from a lightning strike that would

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:12.310
allow Marty to time travel.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:16.460
Together with numerous other Back to the Future
easter eggs in the series, I suspect this

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:21.600
moment is yet another pointer to how time
travel will factor into Season 5, something

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:26.600
I discuss in a lot more detail in my "How
To Beat Vecna" theory video.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.690
When Erica strikes back at Jason's bully friend,
she says…

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:32.860
Crit hit!
…which is a call-back to the winning dice

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:36.250
roll she made in the D&amp;D game at the beginning
of Season 4.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.250
Crit hit!

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:42.570
By the way, that D20 roll which defeated Vecna
in the game will surely also be significant

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:46.199
in how Eleven and the gang eventually defeat
the villain.

00:06:46.199 --> 00:06:51.090
As well as the deliberately Rambo-esque image
in the War Zone's advert, the store's logo

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:53.990
also has a Top Gun vibe about it.

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:57.400
It's an interesting choice given the Tom Cruise
mention this season

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.270
You have a Tom Cruise poster.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.270
That's old.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:05.300
The poster is likely from his Risky Business
era which released in 1983, the year the first

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:06.300
season is set.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.550
Your lover boy from Risky Business.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:09.950
You know, Carol thinks I actually kinda look
like him.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:14.520
Curiously, the Cruise comparisons continue
this season as Mason Dye who plays Jason has

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:20.130
major Tom Cruise vibes and, in fact, he said
he prepared for the role by watching Cruise's

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:21.130
movies.

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:25.770
And inside the War Zone, Jason and his fellow
jocks have plastered the place with 'Wanted'

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.960
posters for Eddie and other members of the
Hellfire Club.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:33.650
The War Zone scene also reminds me of Nancy
and Jonathan stocking up on weapons to do

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:36.150
battle with the Demogorgon in Season 1.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:41.000
The exploding blood balloons that Vecna sets
off when he breaks into Max's memory of the

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:46.300
Snow Ball have vibes of the 2002 adaptation
of Stephen King's novel Carrie where she's

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:51.770
soaked in blood in front of a balloon arch,
as well as the IT miniseries where Pennywise

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:56.530
sets off blood-filled balloons in front of
an adult Richie at the library.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:08:00.950
By the way, the scene in Volume 1 where Eleven
is soaked with a milkshake by Angela's bully

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:05.650
pals in front of everyone at the rink is another
reference to Carrie getting soaked in pig's

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:10.080
blood and laughed at by her peers, an event
that triggers her powers.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.789
Along with Nightmare On Elm Street and IT,
another huge horror influence on both parts

00:08:14.789 --> 00:08:17.729
of Season 4 is Clive Barker's Hellraiser.

00:08:17.729 --> 00:08:22.520
Vecna's attic in the Creel House where he
goes for his creepy meditation sessions has

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:27.240
big Hellraiser vibes as Julia takes Frank's
victims there to feed upon.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:31.590
And the rose window in the door of the Creel
house is also a reference to the stained glass

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:34.230
window in the door of the Hellraiser house.

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:39.340
The Duffer Brothers have also said Vecna is
inspired by Pinhead from the Hellraiser movies,

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:43.920
and despite their quite different appearances
both antagonists have a similar origin in

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:50.090
that they were both once human before transforming
into villains that primarily inhabit an extra-dimensional

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.110
realm.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:55.790
The Michael Myers mask that Eddie puts on
when the crew steal the RV is the same one

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:58.550
that Max wore for Halloween night in Season
2.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:02.320
Red, uh, you got a ski mask or a bandanna,
something like that?

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:07.220
There's also a big Halloween and Michael Myers
easter egg in the way Vecna's body disappears

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:09.830
after he falls through the Creel House attic
window.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:14.790
And I explain that together with even more
easter eggs from the finale such as the Stephen

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:20.700
King book Lucas reads to Max in my Volume
2 ending explained and Season 5 theories video.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.170
You can tap here to watch that or follow the
link in the video description.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:29.540
So, Movie Lovers, what other cool details
or references did you spot in the second part

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:30.540
of Season 4?

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.920
Let me know in the comments below.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:36.950
And if you enjoyed this video, do hit that
like button, I really appreciate it.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:41.640
You can also tap left to discover why I think
Eleven will be time-travelling in Season 5

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.290
in order to defeat Vecna.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:47.440
Thanks for enjoying Stranger Things with me
and hope you have a marvellous movie-loving

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:48.440
week!

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.200
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

